# Ship / release (patch)

When Adam says **commit/push and release a patch** (or similar), do the full path below. Do not stop at commit-only unless he asks.

## Tooling on this Mac

- Repo: `https://github.com/adamcshelton-hub/S2F-Race-Day-Timing` (`origin` on `main`).
- **`gh` is often missing from agent PATH.** Prefer:

```bash
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
```

  Binary lives at `~/.local/bin/gh`. Config: `~/.config/gh/hosts.yml` (user `adamcshelton-hub`). Do not dig the whole home disk for `gh`. Homebrew/`brew` may also be absent from agent shells — do not block on installing them.
- Git HTTPS auth already works via macOS keychain; `git push` and `gh` use that.

## Version bump

1. Read current version from `src/S2F.RaceDayCheckout/S2F.RaceDayCheckout.csproj` (`Version` + `InformationalVersion` — keep them equal).
2. Patch bump both (e.g. `0.5.6` → `0.5.7`). Include the csproj in the same commit as the ship.

## Commit message style

Match recent `main` history:

```text
Ship v0.5.7: short why in one line.

Optional second paragraph with one or two concrete bullets of behavior.
```

Examples on `main`: `Ship v0.5.6: …`, `Ship v0.5.5: …`.

## Push + GitHub Release (required for signed Velopack)

A **tag alone is not enough**. CI uploads signed packs only on a **published** GitHub Release (`release` event in `.github/workflows/build.yml`).

```bash
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
# after commit on main:
git push origin HEAD
git tag v0.5.7          # match Version
git push origin v0.5.7
gh release create v0.5.7 --title "v0.5.7" --notes "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
- Bullet of user-facing change
- Bullet of user-facing change

EOF
)"
```

Return the release URL: `https://github.com/adamcshelton-hub/S2F-Race-Day-Timing/releases/tag/v0.5.7`

## Verify CI

```bash
gh run list --limit 5
# Expect: event=release for vX.Y.Z (pack + Azure Artifact Signing + upload)
# And often a parallel event=push on main
gh run view <id> --json status,conclusion,url
```

Release run must reach **success** before in-app update / installers on the Release page are trustworthy. Main-push packs are CI artifacts only (not the published update channel).

## Do not

- Force-push `main` or move release tags.
- Publish a release just to show a **dev** build on the VM (use `.cursor/rules/vm-dev-launch.mdc`).
- Skip the version bump or ship with mismatched `Version` / tag / release title.
